<h4>2.2 The Council of Nicaea and the Word That Changed Everything</h4>
<p>What did Arius teach, and why did it matter? What does <em>homoousios</em> (consubstantial, "of the same substance") mean, and why was it so important to insist that the Son is "begotten, not made"? If the Son were a creature and not truly God, what would that mean for our salvation?</p>
