<h4>2.3 Trinitarian Analogies: Helpful but Limited</h4>
<p>List three analogies used to help explain the Trinity (e.g., St. Patrick's shamrock, St. Augustine's lover-beloved-love, the family). For each one, identify (a) what it gets right about the Trinity, and (b) where it falls short and could lead to misunderstanding if taken too far.</p>
