<h4>2.6 The Beatitudes: Happiness the Trinitarian Way</h4>
<p>Read Matthew 5:3-10 (the Beatitudes). The world says happiness comes from wealth, power, and comfort; Jesus says happiness comes from poverty of spirit, meekness, mercy, and purity of heart. How does this reversal connect to the Trinitarian pattern of self-giving love? Pick one Beatitude and describe how it reflects the life of the Trinity.</p>
