<h4>E. Attend Mass with Trinitarian Attention</h4>
<p>Attend a Mass this week — Sunday obligation or a weekday Mass — and go with a specific intention: notice every Trinitarian reference. Count how many times the priest prays "through our Lord Jesus Christ, your Son, who lives and reigns with you in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, forever and ever." Notice how the Gloria, the Creed, the Eucharistic Prayer, and the final blessing are all structured. After Mass, write: how many Trinitarian references did you count? Did seeing the liturgy through this lens change your experience of it?</p>
