<section class="content">

<h3>Section 5 &mdash; Verse to Memorize</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all."</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; 2 Corinthians 13:13</p>
</div>

<p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>Tips for memorizing:</strong> Write it by hand three times. Say it aloud slowly, pausing at each of the three gifts: grace (gift of the Son), love (heart of the Father), fellowship (communion of the Spirit). Notice that St. Paul places these three gifts in order: the Son's work (grace), the Father's heart (love), the Spirit's fruit (fellowship). The entire Trinity is present in one sentence.</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Section 6 &mdash; Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>
Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,<br />
God, one and triune,<br />
eternal communion of love.<br />
</p>
<p>
Father, who created me by love —<br />
I praise you for the gift of existence,<br />
for calling me into being not out of necessity but out of generosity.<br />
</p>
<p>
Son, who redeemed me by your cross —<br />
I praise you for becoming flesh, for walking my road,<br />
for dying my death and rising to open the way home.<br />
</p>
<p>
Holy Spirit, who dwells in me —<br />
I praise you for every holy desire, every moment of grace,<br />
for crying out "Abba, Father" in the depths of my heart.<br />
</p>
<p>
Grant that I may live in communion with you and with others;<br />
that I may never seek the solitude of selfishness,<br />
but the joy of shared love;<br />
that my ordinary life — my work, my rest, my relationships —<br />
may become an image of your Trinitarian life.<br />
</p>
<p>
Make room in me, Blessed Trinity.<br />
Let me not keep the empty seat closed,<br />
but welcome you fully — Father, Son, and Holy Spirit —<br />
now and forever.<br />
Amen.
</p>
</blockquote>

